<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Wangara</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Dyula</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Wangara, also known as the Dyula, were Mande-speaking Muslim merchants of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/west-africa">West Africa</a> who organised long-distance trade in gold, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kola-nut">kola nuts</a>, salt and other goods. They established trading communities across the region. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/songhai-empire">Songhai Empire</a> profile notes that Wangara merchants served as the primary long-distance trading intermediaries of the Songhai economy.</p></div>
